{"id": "q0425", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 3.9, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1607, "eot_read_ms": 24, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Provide a bulleted list of things to think about when buying a house", "transcript": "Provide a bulleted list of things to think about when buying a house.", "mode": "local", "answer": "Sure, here’s a list of things to think about when buying a house:\\n\\n- Location and neighborhood safety\\n- Proximity to work, schools, and amenities\\n- Size and layout of the home\\n- Age and condition of the property\\n- Local real estate market trends\\n- Potential for future development in the area\\n- Cost of utilities and property taxes\\n- Space for family needs or hobbies\\n- Accessibility and transportation options\\n- Environmental factors like noise or pollution", "answer_ms": 2649}
{"id": "q0436", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "never", "audio_s": 3.04, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1374, "eot_read_ms": 23, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Why does Daenerys Targaryen want to rule Westeros?", "transcript": "Why does Daenerys Targaryen want to rule Westeros?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Daenerys Targaryen wants to rule Westeros because she believes it is her birthright, as the last surviving heir of the Targaryen dynasty. Raised in exile with her brothers and sister after their father's death, she was taught from a young age that she was destined for greatness and that the Iron Throne was rightfully hers. Her journey across Essos, gathering followers like the Dothraki and forming alliances, stems from this deep-seated belief in her claim. For Daenerys, ruling Westeros isn't just about power—it's about fulfilling her prophecy and restoring what she sees as a rightful legacy.", "answer_ms": 3561}
